All clips 1280×720, 24 fps CFR, H.264 yuv420p, silent, with 12 frames (0.5 s) of movement handle on each end. Cards target 2.5 s opening and 3.0 s ending; narrative cores total 14.5 s; sum is 20.0 s. Editor may use handles for dissolves while preserving the intended running time. `shot-log.json` records measured output counts, movement, and release asset names.

The shot-01 master is the continuity anchor. In shot 2 the blue sleeves and red scarf retain costume identity and the hands have separated from the lantern. Shot 3 presents a downstream reverse view of the same village (church and bridge remain design anchors). Shot 4 retains the lantern on water: it is a tiny warm point within real/reflected stars, not a sky lantern. The end-card plate extends shot 4's star field. Please keep the warm point visible until the final dissolve.

Source stills were visually inspected. Encoded clip inspection and full-decode measurements are recorded in `review.md` and `evidence/technical-checks.json`. This picture handoff is not a finished-film approval.
